  "answer": "6x cos(3x^2 + 1)",
  "mistakes": [],
  "hints": [
    "The outside function is sin(u); the inside function is u = 3x² + 1."
  ],
  "solution": [
    "Outside: $\\frac{d}{du}\\sin u = \\cos u$. Inside: $u = 3x^2 + 1$, $u' = 6x$.",
    "$\\frac{dy}{dx} = \\cos(3x^2+1)\\cdot 6x$."
  ],
  "reference": {
    "book": "openstax-calc1",
    "section": "3.6 The Chain Rule",
    "note": "Original problem."
  },
